ped make the show  a lot more entertaining than it seemed  at first the show won't blow anyone's  minds but it's a decent pick up for the  season especially if you're one who  likes rom-coms  ninth on the list is combatants will be  dispatched  [Music]  okay so listen to this you've got an  obnoxious protagonist who looks like  he's had enough of life on an adventure  besides the straight-laced blonde girl  he's with our protagonist is joined by  an ambitious captain of the god a dark  mage and a chimera with genibio  tendencies if it sounds like some sort  of konosuba love child you're absolutely  correct as it's from the same creator  from an anecdotal standpoint it seems  that when it comes to fantasy the same  court of archetypes and personalities to  form that specific four or five person  party has proven to work excellently i  mean you do see shades of it in the core  cast of ari furetha princess connect has  something resembling it too they all  differ in execution and for combatants  who will be dispatched that comes in the  form of some tactical warfare gimmicks  and a heavy focus on lewd comedy if  you're up for something like gonosuba  and want more of the laughs and the  degeneracy from it combatants should be  part of your watch list no question  at number eight we take a look at  shadows house  shadow's house is an interesting show  before the season started i praised its  overall ambiance in its victorian era  backdrop i felt that we're due for  another creepy gothic anime and so far i  think that my expectations for shadow's  house have been met the mysteries are  great and i had my ample full of  suspense from this anime and while i  wouldn't put shadow's house as anime of  the season candidate i think the  cloverworks has done an overall  excellent job in bringing the series to  life seriously it just does such a good  job at captivating the audience with  those eerie supernatural elements in the  overall cinematography you get drawn  into the mystery of the shadow's house  and like a spectre the anime just  doesn't let you go once it's in your  grass i can't wait to see more with each  passing episode and as more questions  appear with everyone that gets answered  if you're like me and if you're looking  for something chilly and mysterious this  season has this great anime for you  [Music]  seventh in line is don't toy with me  miss nagatoro  [Music]  it's a show that i braced myself for  early on in the season but surprisingly  the reception towards nagatoro has been  pretty taped i admit that seeing  nakathora's smug face for the first few  episodes was quite addictive and i think  that in terms of the production side of  things the show is serviceable the  acting's great and i think that the art  is just right for a show like this i  can't help but feel sorry for the poor  guy though the show has been getting a  steady increase in his fan base through  the anime adaptation and i think that a  lot of it has to do with the characters  and their antics we've seen the bullying  turning into romance thing before still  i don't think that makes it a bad show  if you're looking for a rom-com with  that premise nagatoro should suffice in  giving you your fill for the season  number six on the list is higahiro  kajimoto  here's another winner that i admittedly  overlooked before the season started i  mean i figured that the premise might  not be everyone's cup of tea but after  watching the first few eps and reading  some of the source material i'd say that  higahiro is one of the best romances  that we have this season i'd also say  that you should give the show a chance  because when you do it does shine in a  lot of ways it seems the past few years  the parent-child dynamic in anime has  been gaining some momentum despite the  premise possibly setting off some red  flags i don't find anything too  questionable about the series yep  there's some minor fan service in there  but come on are we still piling about 