evive mecca into the mainstream well  not really however what it does provide  is an excellent story that i feel  perfectly fits the current state of the  times i don't really want to go too  political but when looking at the  content of 86 it does have those  undertones hidden underneath the  gripping story of hardship and  perseverance it has a lot to do with the  status quo and the class differences  between citizens some racial conflict  and some surprisingly deep ideas about  military might and what at first glance  could look like a seasonal popcorn flick  that's not even mentioning an amazing  soundtrack presented by the legendary  hiroyuki sawano 86 is a winner for the  season you should definitely check it  out  when the season started i honestly  didn't know what to expect from vv it  looked appealing enough and i wanted to  watch sci-fi and it's done by the guys  who gave us re-zero but expectations  were rather tempered when i look back  well it turns out that what we have here  is a strong candidate for animate of the  season just like 86 before it i feel  that vivi has a bevy of strong themes  mostly to do with morals politics and  the fight against fate however we all  know casual watchers typically aren't  immediately drawn to a series through  those themes right so for that bb has  its spectacular visuals amazing  soundtrack and a fast-paced execution of  the story it's very eye-catching to say  the least even having one of my favorite  anime fights that feature female  characters and there's more on that on  the other video that i'll be linking  overall i'd say that this anime is  amazing if you like sci-fi animators  action-packed and way more than just  your usual popcorn flick give vivi a  shop i know you're going to enjoy it  number two for our list is to your  eternity  now here's a show that was a no-brainer  for inclusion to the preseason list it  seems that everyone's hyped for the show  and what do you know it didn't  disappoint one bit it